// Dynamic sequence view: fanning out a message to a participant on another Velox instance.
//
// Assumes an established federated group — all member credentials are already embedded
// in the shared ratchet tree on both sides. No Identity call needed per commit.
//
// Federation trust layers:
//   - mutual TLS — MIMI-conformant channel + hostname authentication (WIP)
//   - ed25519 instance signing key — hop-independent payload authenticity
// Hub model (MIMI): per chat, a single home instance is the HUB. Defaults to the
// chat-creator's instance; changes only via explicit hub-transfer state events.
// This diagram assumes the LOCAL instance is the hub. (Non-hub flow: local client's
// op is forwarded to the peer hub via Interconnect before commit.)

views {
  dynamic view flowFederatedMessage {
    title "Flows / Send Message (Federated)"
    description '''
      Covers the outbound leg when a chat has participants on another Velox instance and
      THIS instance is the hub. The client constructs the MLS commit; Delivery serialises
      it via the Valkey epoch lease and publishes both a local messages event and a
      federation-egress event to Kafka. Interconnect picks up federation-egress, signs the
      payload with the instance ed25519 key, and POSTs it to the peer's Federation Edge
      over mutual TLS. The peer's Edge verifies the signature and routes to its own
      Delivery via the MIMI `/notify` endpoint.

      ---

      **Federation** — Matrix-style replication. Interconnect forwards MLS commits to peer
      Velox instances; the peer re-publishes them to its local `messages` topic.

      **Ratchet tree** — MLS group state shared across all instances when the group was formed
      or last updated. Contains every member's credential at their leaf node. No per-commit
      credential fetch is needed — both sides already have it.

      **federation-egress** — Kafka topic produced by Delivery when a message must reach a
      peer. Interconnect consumes it, signs the payload with the instance ed25519 key, and
      POSTs to the peer's Federation Edge over mTLS.

      **ed25519** — Edwards-curve digital signature scheme. Each Velox instance signs outbound
      federation payloads with its private key; the public key is in `.well-known/velox/server`.
      Peer instances verify signatures independently of the TLS hop — defence in depth over
      mTLS.

      **DNS SRV + .well-known** — How Interconnect discovers a peer: `_velox._tcp.<domain>`
      SRV record gives the endpoint; `.well-known/velox/server` (migrating to
      `.well-known/mimi-protocol-directory` — WIP) provides the ed25519 public key.

      **Hub (MIMI, WIP)** — The Velox instance responsible for ordering MLS commits for a
      given chat. Defaults to the chat-creator's instance; changes only via an explicit
      hub-transfer state event. Replaces the earlier dynamic "leader election" language.

      **Federation Edge** — Peer's inbound gateway. Terminates mTLS, verifies our ed25519
      signature, and routes `/notify` / `/update` to the peer's Delivery.

      **MIMI endpoints (WIP)** — The outbound POST targets `/notify/{roomId}` on the peer's
      Federation Edge per draft-ietf-mimi-protocol. Names and wire format may change before
      the spec is finalised.
    '''
    variant sequence

    velox.webUI -[realtime]-> velox.deliveryService "request epoch lease (WebTransport)"
    velox.deliveryService -> velox.deliveryValkey "CAS: issue epoch N lease to client"
    velox.webUI <- velox.deliveryService "epoch N lease granted"
    velox.webUI -> velox.webUI "construct MLS Commit for epoch N (client-side)"
    velox.webUI -[realtime]-> velox.deliveryService "submit commit + ciphertext (WebTransport)"
    velox.deliveryService -> velox.deliveryValkey "CAS: advance epoch N → N+1 (lease released)"
    parallel {
      velox.deliveryService -[async]-> velox.kafka "publish → messages topic (local fan-out)"
      velox.deliveryService -[async]-> velox.kafka "publish → federation-egress topic"
    }
    velox.webUI <- velox.deliveryService "ACK (epoch N committed)"

    // Local fan-out (same as local-chat flow)
    velox.kafka -> velox.storeService "consume messages"
    velox.storeService -> velox.scylla "persist MLS commit + ciphertext"
    velox.kafka -> velox.deliveryService "consume messages"
    velox.deliveryService -[realtime]-> velox.webUI "push to local online recipients"

    // Federated leg — no Identity call needed; ratchet tree on both sides already has credentials
    velox.kafka -> velox.interconnectService "consume federation-egress"
    velox.interconnectService -> dns "SRV lookup + .well-known (MIMI directory path — WIP)"
    velox.interconnectService <- dns "peer Federation Edge endpoint + ed25519 signing key"
    velox.interconnectService -> otherVelox "POST /notify/{roomId} — ed25519-signed MLS commit (mTLS, MIMI — WIP)"
    velox.interconnectService <- otherVelox "ACK (peer Edge verified signature and routed to peer Delivery)"
  }
}
